APPENDIX: DETAILED MONTHLY PAYMENT CALCULATIONS







Mathematical Verification:



Total Amount to be Repaid:

• Original Investment: $4,000,000

• ROI (40% of $4M): $1,600,000

• Total Repayment Amount: $5,600,000



Monthly Payment Calculation:

• Total Repayment ÷ Payment Period = Monthly Payment

• $5,600,000 ÷ 36 months = $155,555.56 per month



Payment Breakdown:

• Principal Component: $4,000,000 ÷ 36 = $111,111.11/month

• ROI Component: $1,600,000 ÷ 36 = $44,444.44/month

• Total Monthly Payment: $155,555.55/month



Annual Payment Requirements:

• Monthly Payment × 12 = $1,866,666 annually

• This represents 23% of Year 1 revenue ($8M)

• This represents 5% of Year 2 revenue ($38M)

• This represents 1.4% of Year 3 revenue ($130M)



The corrected calculations demonstrate that the investment becomes increasingly manageable as the business scales, validating the underlying business model while ensuring accurate financial planning and investor expectations.